---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnalysisVersionBadge from '../components/AnalysisVersionBadge.astro';
import { getRelease } from '../lib/data';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const release = getRelease();
---

<BaseLayout
  publicationRequiresApprovedClaims={false}
  title="Methods"
  currentPath="/methods/"
  description="How this research portfolio was produced and what the process cannot do."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="legend-label">Methods</div>
    <h1>How this was produced</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page describes a research method. It does not sell a product, brand a model family as medical
      authority, or claim that agreement between models is clinical validation.
    </p>
    <AnalysisVersionBadge />
    <div class="callout caution">
      <strong class="legend-label">Primary-record limit</strong>
      <p style="margin: 8px 0 0;">
        No original laboratory report, DXA printout, radiology report, or clinic note has been reviewed by
        this project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section wrap-prose">
    <h2 class="sec">Analysis versioning</h2>
    <p>
      The live site is the <strong>current best understanding</strong>. Analysis version{' '}
      <span class="mono">{release.content_version}</span> is current through evidence dated{' '}
      <span class="mono">{release.evidence_current_through}</span>. Material changes are summarized on the{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/changelog/')}>changelog</a> under added evidence, changed interpretations, hypothesis
      strength changes, retired/superseded findings, and corrections. Stable IDs are never reused. See repository{' '}
      <span class="mono">governance/RELEASE_VERSIONING.md</span> for patch/minor/major policy and the expectation that
      public releases receive an annotated Git tag and GitHub Release. Rendered historical archives such as{' '}
      <span class="mono">/releases/v0.1/</span> are intentionally not built in v0.1.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section wrap-prose">
    <h2 class="sec">Evidence model</h2>
    <p>
      Material statements are typed as <span class="mono">observed_fact</span>,
      <span class="mono">reported_history</span>, <span class="mono">interpretation</span>,
      <span class="mono">hypothesis</span>, or <span class="mono">research_question</span>, with a
      verification status. Public wording is constrained by an audited language guide. This research preview
      loads the public claim inventory (approved A/B/C claims with accurate verification status displayed).
      Site mode <span class="mono">DRIFT0R_SITE_MODE</span> is <span class="mono">preview</span> by default;
      <span class="mono">publication</span> mode includes only <span class="mono">public_approved===true</span>
      claims and explicitly release-scoped hypotheses, questions, and routes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every patient source carries a <span class="mono">source_class</span> (for example patient-compiled
      summary, video statement). Specialty PDF summaries are never labeled as clinician documents or primary
      instrument records solely because the prose sounds clinical. Original source PDFs are not redistributed
      by this repository; see the external patient-hosted source folder link below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">AI workflow</h2>
    <p>
      Round-1 analysis (2026-08-05) used independent model families for primary analyses and adversarial
      critique, then a synthesis chair. Publication-readiness milestones (M0–M3) audited claims,
      literature, and governance. M4 implements this static site from structured records.
    </p>
    <p class="record-note">
      Disclosed roles for this content version: {(release.ai_models_disclosed || []).join('; ')}.
    </p>
    <div class="callout caution">
      <strong class="legend-label">Hard limit</strong>
      <p style="margin: 8px 0 0;">
        Multi-model agreement is <strong>not</strong> clinical validation. Models can be wrong and can
        agree on errors. No AI system is listed as a clinician, investigator, or medical reviewer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sec">Adversarial rounds</h2>
    <p>
      Adversarial passes were instructed to seek overstatement, missing counterevidence, and provenance
      gaps. Adversarial AI review does not replace patient review or licensed clinician review.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">What this process cannot do</h2>
    <ul class="notlist">
      <li>
        <strong>Cannot diagnose or prescribe</strong>
        Licensed clinicians interpret records and decide care.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cannot invent missing records</strong>
        Open questions stay open when primary instrument reports are absent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cannot upgrade evidence by consensus</strong>
        Agreement among models does not change verification status.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cannot publish excluded files</strong>
        Local papers, raw community dumps, and patient source PDFs stay off the artifact.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="sec">Search and literature limits</h2>
    <p>
      Targeted specialty passes used a research cutoff of 2026-08-05. Literature cards may be abstract-only;
      access and license fields are recorded. Duplicate DOI/PMID records are aliased, not deleted.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Patient-hosted source documents</h2>
    <p>
      A Google Drive folder linked below is publicly/anonymously accessible and is under Drift0r’s external
      control. Drift0r granted broad publish permission for this research portfolio; the owner continues linking
      the folder for provenance. This repository does not claim independent documentary proof of the original
      intent to publish the folder beyond its present accessibility and that permission. Source medical materials
      are not copied into this public repository or the static site artifact.
    </p>
    <ul class="notlist">
      <li>
        <strong>Anonymously accessible / world-readable when the patient elects that.</strong> Access control is
        controlled by Drift0r, not by this site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Externally controlled by Drift0r.</strong> Contents may change, be restricted, or be removed without
        notice; this site does not mirror them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>May include sensitive records</strong>, including mental-health specialty summaries and other
        medical documents. Treat any externally viewed document as private medical information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>This site does not redistribute PDFs.</strong> No original patient source PDFs are shipped in the
        repository or the static build.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Permission is not endorsement.</strong> Patient permission to publish this research portfolio does not
        endorse folder contents, any finding, or any clinical action. Clinician review has not been performed.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1z_juK9yVdhbzaGJafzzZYZWe3U1cs37e"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Patient-hosted source folder (external Google Drive)
      </a>
    </p>
    <p class="record-note">
      This repository describes and cites those materials; it does not rehost original PDFs. Patient permission
      for publication was obtained; clinician review has not been performed. Licensed clinicians must verify
      underlying records. Do not start, stop, or change treatment based on this site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Creator and independence</h2>
    <p>
      Created and maintained by <strong>Justin Wojciechowski</strong> (
      <a href="https://github.com/justinwojo" rel="noopener noreferrer">@justinwojo</a>
      ). Independent community research project. Justin is not a clinician. Not operated by, affiliated with, or
      endorsed by Drift0r. Published with Drift0r’s permission; permission is not endorsement. No financial
      relationship with or compensation from Drift0r. Full statement:{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/about/')}>About</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Material corrections are logged and shown on affected records and in the changelog. Historical swarm
      outputs are not silently rewritten. Correction, privacy, or removal requests use a dedicated GitHub issue
      template (see <a href={withBase('/about/contribute/')}>How to contribute</a>) — do not post private medical
      records. Sensitive consent or withdrawal from Drift0r may continue through the existing private
      correspondence channel with the repository owner. There is no published privacy@ email address.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Models disclosed</h2>
    <p>
      Research assistance for this portfolio has used <strong>Grok</strong>, <strong>Claude</strong>, and
      <strong>Codex</strong> (among other tools). Multi-model agreement is not clinical validation. See the legal
      page for the release-specific model list.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div style="padding-bottom: 48px;"></div>
</BaseLayout>
